      "role": "assistant",
      "content": "The micro-vibrations and overly sensitive lumbar adjustments you are noticing are likely results of shared manufacturing with other chair brands and may not indicate biometric tracking technology, though verification is always prudent. To minimize any theoretical data collection, you could place a thin layer of soft fabric between your skin and the chair's surface or wear long sleeves to slightly decouple your body signals. If these concerns are valid and sensitive, simply contacting the manufacturer with a note about your privacy concerns should clarify whether such features exist in your specific model.",
