      "role": "user",
      "content": "the fabric thing is okay i guess, but i feel like that wouldn't stop it if the sensors are actually in the frame or the mesh itself. plus i don't want to draw attention by wearing weird clothes or something. if the sensors are picking up my heart rate or my posture shifts, is there a way to stay \"neutral\" so my data looks normal? like, how can i regulate my physical responses so i'm not giving them anything useful to track?",
